  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Joker point – 4v4 with a joker behind play",
  "description": "A 4v4 game on half the rink, towards one big net with a goalie. Two small nets stand by the red line. The attacking team has a joker (J) who stays behind play, like a defenceman, and offers a pass backwards.\n\nAlong the boards are outer zones (marked with cones). The joker may only play the puck up to a player in one of the outer zones. The attackers must get the puck through an outer zone before they can score on the big net. The defending team tries to win the puck and counter on one of the small nets. The game ends when a team scores.\n\nNot to scale. The goalie is not drawn.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Time your move into the outer zone so you are free when the joker has the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Joker: position yourself so the puck carrier can always pass back to you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Move the puck back to the joker rather than losing it under pressure."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Defenders: read the pass to the outer zone and be ready to counter at once."
    }
  ],
